{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionSU3BracketClosure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionSU3BracketClosure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionSU3Stabilizer","lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.ColourStabilizerAction"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.ColourStabilizerActionOnSU3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.ColourStabilizerActionOnSU3","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionSU3BracketClosure.lean#L95-L104","doc":"**The concrete colour-action conjecture** (bean `qou-iibg`): the\nappendix class `ColourStabilizerAction` specialised to the corpus's\noctonion stabilizer `su3 e`. **No instance is provided** — producing one\n(a faithful linear action of `su3 e` on the 3-strand state space) is the\nopen derivation recorded by `conj:sm-colour-stabilizer-action`; by\n`colour_needs_three_strands` any host `V` must have `finrank ℚ V ≥ 3`\nwhenever `finrank ℚ (su3 e) = 8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.instModuleSU3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.instModuleSU3","kind":"instance","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionSU3BracketClosure.lean#L91-L93","doc":"Companion `Module` registration, for the same nesting reason. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.instAddCommGroupSU3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.instAddCommGroupSU3","kind":"instance","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionSU3BracketClosure.lean#L85-L89","doc":"The standard `AddCommGroup` structure on the stabilizer subtype,\nregistered with a direct head key so importers resolve it at the default\n`maxSynthPendingDepth` (see the option comment at the top of this file). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.bracketDer_mem_su3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.bracketDer_mem_su3","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionSU3BracketClosure.lean#L74-L83","doc":"**Bracket closure of the colour stabilizer** (bean `qou-51st`): if `D₁`\nand `D₂` both kill `e` then so does their commutator —\n`[D₁,D₂] e = D₁ (D₂ e) − D₂ (D₁ e) = D₁ 0 − D₂ 0 = 0`. Together with\n`bracket_mem_Der𝕆` this exhibits `su3 e` as a Lie subalgebra of\n`Der(𝕆) = 𝔤₂`, as the Günaydin–Gürsey colour picture requires. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.bracketDer_coe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.bracketDer_coe","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionSU3BracketClosure.lean#L70-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.bracketDer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.bracketDer","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionSU3BracketClosure.lean#L66-L68","doc":"The commutator bracket on the derivation algebra `Der𝕆 = 𝔤₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.bracket_mem_Der𝕆","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.bracket_mem_Der𝕆","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionSU3BracketClosure.lean#L60-L64","doc":"`Der𝕆` is closed under the commutator bracket. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.bracket_mem_ker_leibnizDefect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.bracket_mem_ker_leibnizDefect","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionSU3BracketClosure.lean#L44-L56","doc":"**Derivations are closed under the commutator** (generic): for any\nbilinear multiplication `m`, if `D₁, D₂` satisfy the Leibniz rule then so\ndoes `D₁ ∘ D₂ − D₂ ∘ D₁` — the second-order cross terms cancel. ","signatureChunk":0}]}